2. **D-EX-GRANT-EPOCH-NOT-UNIQUE-TENURE-ID (#15, the named blocker for #1's gate swap): full code audit done, and the ledger's fix list turns out mostly stale** — steps 1/2/4 (the +1 sequence `caw_next_grant_epoch`, tombstone/claim epoch carry, single explicit-grantee mint point) already landed in sess108 and are on the rig. Remaining: the tuple-validation audit and a wrap-boundary verification test. The audit inventoried all 8 mint sites and every holder-bit install, and found one real design hazard: **the mint fires on every write-capable grant image, so a same-node PW→EX upgrade re-mints mid-tenure**, which under a future equality-gated replay would wrongly refuse legitimately-durable same-tenure records (latent — XFS never uses PW today). Two sites live in a `__maybe_unused` function whose liveness needs one grep. All of this plus the injection-test design (via the existing `caw_inject_*` framework) is queued for a RULE-5 consult at the start of next session.

3. **Memory compaction started**: a background agent is folding the 20-note sess112-125 waiter-cancel campaign into `compiled-samenode-waiter-cancel-campaign`; next session must verify the article exists with all 20 slugs cited (procedure in the session note).

